  38:./ucos/Core/os_sem.c **** /*
  39:./ucos/Core/os_sem.c **** ***************************************************************************************************
  40:./ucos/Core/os_sem.c **** *                                          ACCEPT SEMAPHORE
  41:./ucos/Core/os_sem.c **** *
  42:./ucos/Core/os_sem.c **** * Description: This function checks the semaphore to see if a resource is available or, if an event
  43:./ucos/Core/os_sem.c **** *              occurred.  Unlike OSSemPend(), OSSemAccept() does not suspend the calling task if th
  44:./ucos/Core/os_sem.c **** *              resource is not available or the event did not occur.
  45:./ucos/Core/os_sem.c **** *
  46:./ucos/Core/os_sem.c **** * Arguments  : pevent     is a pointer to the event control block
  47:./ucos/Core/os_sem.c **** *
  48:./ucos/Core/os_sem.c **** * Returns    : >  0       if the resource is available or the event did not occur the semaphore is
  49:./ucos/Core/os_sem.c **** *                         decremented to obtain the resource.
  50:./ucos/Core/os_sem.c **** *              == 0       if the resource is not available or the event did not occur or,
  51:./ucos/Core/os_sem.c **** *                         if 'pevent' is a NULL pointer or,
  52:./ucos/Core/os_sem.c **** *                         if you didn't pass a pointer to a semaphore
  53:./ucos/Core/os_sem.c **** ***************************************************************************************************
  54:./ucos/Core/os_sem.c **** */
