  85:./ucos/Core/os_sem.c **** /*
  86:./ucos/Core/os_sem.c **** ***************************************************************************************************
  87:./ucos/Core/os_sem.c **** *                                         CREATE A SEMAPHORE
  88:./ucos/Core/os_sem.c **** *
  89:./ucos/Core/os_sem.c **** * Description: This function creates a semaphore.
  90:./ucos/Core/os_sem.c **** *
  91:./ucos/Core/os_sem.c **** * Arguments  : cnt           is the initial value for the semaphore.  If the value is 0, no resourc
  92:./ucos/Core/os_sem.c **** *                            available (or no event has occurred).  You initialize the semaphore to
  93:./ucos/Core/os_sem.c **** *                            non-zero value to specify how many resources are available (e.g. if yo
  94:./ucos/Core/os_sem.c **** *                            10 resources, you would initialize the semaphore to 10).
  95:./ucos/Core/os_sem.c **** *
  96:./ucos/Core/os_sem.c **** * Returns    : != (void *)0  is a pointer to the event control block (OS_EVENT) associated with the
  97:./ucos/Core/os_sem.c **** *                            created semaphore
  98:./ucos/Core/os_sem.c **** *              == (void *)0  if no event control blocks were available
  99:./ucos/Core/os_sem.c **** ***************************************************************************************************
 100:./ucos/Core/os_sem.c **** */
