 141:./ucos/Core/os_sem.c **** /*
 142:./ucos/Core/os_sem.c **** ***************************************************************************************************
 143:./ucos/Core/os_sem.c **** *                                         DELETE A SEMAPHORE
 144:./ucos/Core/os_sem.c **** *
 145:./ucos/Core/os_sem.c **** * Description: This function deletes a semaphore and readies all tasks pending on the semaphore.
 146:./ucos/Core/os_sem.c **** *
 147:./ucos/Core/os_sem.c **** * Arguments  : pevent        is a pointer to the event control block associated with the desired
 148:./ucos/Core/os_sem.c **** *                            semaphore.
 149:./ucos/Core/os_sem.c **** *
 150:./ucos/Core/os_sem.c **** *              opt           determines delete options as follows:
 151:./ucos/Core/os_sem.c **** *                            opt == OS_DEL_NO_PEND   Delete semaphore ONLY if no task pending
 152:./ucos/Core/os_sem.c **** *                            opt == OS_DEL_ALWAYS    Deletes the semaphore even if tasks are waitin
 153:./ucos/Core/os_sem.c **** *                                                    In this case, all the tasks pending will be re
 154:./ucos/Core/os_sem.c **** *
 155:./ucos/Core/os_sem.c **** *              perr          is a pointer to an error code that can contain one of the following va
 156:./ucos/Core/os_sem.c **** *                            OS_ERR_NONE                  The call was successful and the semaphore
 157:./ucos/Core/os_sem.c **** *                                                         deleted
 158:./ucos/Core/os_sem.c **** *                            OS_ERR_DEL_ISR               If you attempted to delete the semaphore 
 159:./ucos/Core/os_sem.c **** *                                                         ISR
 160:./ucos/Core/os_sem.c **** *                            OS_ERR_ILLEGAL_DEL_RUN_TIME  If you tried to delete the semaphore afte
 161:./ucos/Core/os_sem.c **** *                                                         safety critical operation started.
