 290:./ucos/Core/os_sem.c **** ***************************************************************************************************
 291:./ucos/Core/os_sem.c **** *                                          PEND ON SEMAPHORE
 292:./ucos/Core/os_sem.c **** *
 293:./ucos/Core/os_sem.c **** * Description: This function waits for a semaphore.
 294:./ucos/Core/os_sem.c **** *
ARM GAS  /tmp/ccAvEVGU.s 			page 16


 295:./ucos/Core/os_sem.c **** * Arguments  : pevent        is a pointer to the event control block associated with the desired
 296:./ucos/Core/os_sem.c **** *                            semaphore.
 297:./ucos/Core/os_sem.c **** *
 298:./ucos/Core/os_sem.c **** *              timeout       is an optional timeout period (in clock ticks).  If non-zero, your tas
 299:./ucos/Core/os_sem.c **** *                            wait for the resource up to the amount of time specified by this argum
 300:./ucos/Core/os_sem.c **** *                            If you specify 0, however, your task will wait forever at the specifie
 301:./ucos/Core/os_sem.c **** *                            semaphore or, until the resource becomes available (or the event occur
 302:./ucos/Core/os_sem.c **** *
 303:./ucos/Core/os_sem.c **** *              perr          is a pointer to where an error message will be deposited.  Possible er
 304:./ucos/Core/os_sem.c **** *                            messages are:
 305:./ucos/Core/os_sem.c **** *
 306:./ucos/Core/os_sem.c **** *                            OS_ERR_NONE         The call was successful and your task owns the res
 307:./ucos/Core/os_sem.c **** *                                                or, the event you are waiting for occurred.
 308:./ucos/Core/os_sem.c **** *                            OS_ERR_TIMEOUT      The semaphore was not received within the specifie
 309:./ucos/Core/os_sem.c **** *                                                'timeout'.
 310:./ucos/Core/os_sem.c **** *                            OS_ERR_PEND_ABORT   The wait on the semaphore was aborted.
 311:./ucos/Core/os_sem.c **** *                            OS_ERR_EVENT_TYPE   If you didn't pass a pointer to a semaphore.
 312:./ucos/Core/os_sem.c **** *                            OS_ERR_PEND_ISR     If you called this function from an ISR and the re
 313:./ucos/Core/os_sem.c **** *                                                would lead to a suspension.
 314:./ucos/Core/os_sem.c **** *                            OS_ERR_PEVENT_NULL  If 'pevent' is a NULL pointer.
 315:./ucos/Core/os_sem.c **** *                            OS_ERR_PEND_LOCKED  If you called this function when the scheduler is 
 316:./ucos/Core/os_sem.c **** *
 317:./ucos/Core/os_sem.c **** * Returns    : none
 318:./ucos/Core/os_sem.c **** ***************************************************************************************************
 319:./ucos/Core/os_sem.c **** */
