 405:./ucos/Core/os_sem.c **** /*
 406:./ucos/Core/os_sem.c **** ***************************************************************************************************
 407:./ucos/Core/os_sem.c **** *                                    ABORT WAITING ON A SEMAPHORE
 408:./ucos/Core/os_sem.c **** *
 409:./ucos/Core/os_sem.c **** * Description: This function aborts & readies any tasks currently waiting on a semaphore.  This fun
 410:./ucos/Core/os_sem.c **** *              should be used to fault-abort the wait on the semaphore, rather than to normally sig
 411:./ucos/Core/os_sem.c **** *              the semaphore via OSSemPost().
 412:./ucos/Core/os_sem.c **** *
 413:./ucos/Core/os_sem.c **** * Arguments  : pevent        is a pointer to the event control block associated with the desired
 414:./ucos/Core/os_sem.c **** *                            semaphore.
 415:./ucos/Core/os_sem.c **** *
 416:./ucos/Core/os_sem.c **** *              opt           determines the type of ABORT performed:
 417:./ucos/Core/os_sem.c **** *                            OS_PEND_OPT_NONE         ABORT wait for a single task (HPT) waiting on
 418:./ucos/Core/os_sem.c **** *                                                     semaphore
 419:./ucos/Core/os_sem.c **** *                            OS_PEND_OPT_BROADCAST    ABORT wait for ALL tasks that are  waiting on
 420:./ucos/Core/os_sem.c **** *                                                     semaphore
 421:./ucos/Core/os_sem.c **** *
 422:./ucos/Core/os_sem.c **** *              perr          is a pointer to where an error message will be deposited.  Possible er
 423:./ucos/Core/os_sem.c **** *                            messages are:
 424:./ucos/Core/os_sem.c **** *
 425:./ucos/Core/os_sem.c **** *                            OS_ERR_NONE         No tasks were     waiting on the semaphore.
 426:./ucos/Core/os_sem.c **** *                            OS_ERR_PEND_ABORT   At least one task waiting on the semaphore was rea
 427:./ucos/Core/os_sem.c **** *                                                and informed of the aborted wait; check return val
 428:./ucos/Core/os_sem.c **** *                                                for the number of tasks whose wait on the semaphor
 429:./ucos/Core/os_sem.c **** *                                                was aborted.
 430:./ucos/Core/os_sem.c **** *                            OS_ERR_EVENT_TYPE   If you didn't pass a pointer to a semaphore.
 431:./ucos/Core/os_sem.c **** *                            OS_ERR_PEVENT_NULL  If 'pevent' is a NULL pointer.
 432:./ucos/Core/os_sem.c **** *
 433:./ucos/Core/os_sem.c **** * Returns    : == 0          if no tasks were waiting on the semaphore, or upon error.
 434:./ucos/Core/os_sem.c **** *              >  0          if one or more tasks waiting on the semaphore are now readied and info
 435:./ucos/Core/os_sem.c **** ***************************************************************************************************
 436:./ucos/Core/os_sem.c **** */
 437:./ucos/Core/os_sem.c **** 
 438:./ucos/Core/os_sem.c **** #if OS_SEM_PEND_ABORT_EN > 0u
